{
  "_readme": [
    "Companion to dark.json. Both shipped themes are kept COMPLETE (full key",
    "parity with the reference) so sync-theme.js's parity gate can lint them",
    "against each other. Drop-in themes are the partial case: once the loader",
    "merges over dark.json, a user theme may define as few keys as it likes.",
    "",
    "base: 'light' -> the loader emits data-theme-base=\"light\". CSS that must",
    "branch on light vs dark (icon assets, image filters) keys off THAT, never",
    "off data-theme, which carries the theme id and cannot be enumerated once",
    "themes are user-supplied.",
    "",
    "Values are NOT a mechanical inversion of dark.json. Anything drawn over",
    "the 2D canvas (render2d.background #cdcdcd) or the 3D viewport",
    "(render3d.background #e8eaed) needs luminance well below the surface it",
    "sits on, so saturated high-luminance hues from the dark palette (#00ffff,",
    "#ffff00, #44ff88) are darkened here rather than copied."
  ],

  "id": "light",
  "label": "Light",
  "base": "light",
  "description": "Default light theme.",
  "author": "Eltryus - Ricardo Marques",
  "license": "AGPL-3.0-or-later",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/RicardoJCMarques/EasyCAM5000",

